# bioinformatics - table data: the reference data the rest of the deck reads.
# Spliced into bioinformatics.j via include - not a standalone module.
#
# GENERATED by tools/gentables.j. The alternative genetic codes are emitted
# as full literal maps because a const read costs nothing while a per-call
# construction does (examples/bench.j). What a reviewer needs to check is not
# 64 lines of near-identical data but the handful of codons each table
# reassigns - tables_test.j holds exactly that difference list and fails if a
# table here stops matching it.

/**
 * NCBI genetic code 1 - Standard.
 *
 * The eukaryotic nuclear code, and the deck's default everywhere a
 * genetic code is not named explicitly.
 *
 * @see https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Taxonomy/Utils/wprintgc.cgi#SG1
 */
export def const STANDARD as map of string to string init {
    "TTT": "F",
